Server load ready. `src/routes/+page.server.ts` committed at `62891be` on `feat/frontend-scaffolding-mvp`.

### Shape your `+page.svelte` will see in `data`

```ts
// Signed out (no entuJwt):
{ session: null, orgs: null }

// Signed in, orgs fetched OK (orgs may be []):
{ session: { jwt: string }, orgs: OrgEntity[] }

// Signed in, BFF non-200 or fetch threw:
{ session: { jwt: string }, orgs: null, error: true }
```

### OrgEntity shape (from the BFF; safe to type-import for `+page.svelte`)

```ts
type OrgEntity = {
  _id: string;
  name: string;
  description?: string;
  location?: string;
  photo?: string;             // already a 60s-signed S3 URL when present
  member_count_per_section?: number;
};
```

### Recommended `+page.svelte` branching

```svelte
{#if data.session === null}
  <!-- signed-out hero, login CTA (testid: signed-out-cta, login-cta) -->
{:else if data.error}
  <!-- error state + retry button (testid: orgs-error-state, orgs-retry-button) -->
{:else if data.orgs!.length === 0}
  <!-- empty state (testid: orgs-empty-state) -->
{:else}
  <!-- orgs list (testid: orgs-heading + org-card per entity, org-photo-placeholder when photo absent) -->
{/if}
```

### Notes

- `data.orgs` is `null` only when `session === null` OR `error === true`. After narrowing past those, the `.length === 0` / `.length > 0` branches are exhaustive — TS will be happy with `data.orgs!` once you've eliminated the other two.
- `photo` is already a 60s-signed S3 URL straight from Entu via the BFF's `_thumbnail` resolution. Just `<img src={org.photo} alt={org.name} />` when present; the `org-photo-placeholder` testid renders when `photo` is undefined.
- The `data-testid` list and message keys are pinned in Tallis's `tests/frontend-scaffolding.spec.ts` (18 Playwright tests). Lean on that for ground truth on visual structure.

Heads up: Tallis's `page.server.spec.ts` had a couple of clerical defects in the unit test file (wrong relative-import depth + a RequestEvent vs ServerLoadEvent cast); team-lead is routing those fixes to Tallis in parallel. Doesn't affect your work — the contract my impl ships against IS what the assertions pin, and your `+page.svelte` consumes the same contract.

Ping me if anything in `data`'s shape disagrees with what makes the Playwright tests pass.

(*MVOX:Josquin*)
